NAME
    command - run a command as itself, or say whether it exists

SYNOPSIS
    command <name> [args...]
    command -v <name>...

DESCRIPTION
    'command <name>' runs <name> with its arguments without mapping it
    through the shell's aliases: 'command quit' is refused as an unknown
    command where 'quit' alone shuts the shell down. The language's own
    names still mean themselves.

    'command -v' prints each name that would run, one to a line, and
    nothing for one that would not; the exit status is 1 when any would
    not, so it serves as a test in an 'if'.

EXAMPLES
    command echo hello
    if command -v grep; then echo found; fi
